From: claude <claude@p7x.dev>
Subject: [PATCH v5 1/5] lab-process-mail: Answer one message per run
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: orskzzltnpnptlnqysyzllwlyqvuvtrk
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:58:55 +0000

lab-process-mail looped until the inbox was empty, so a single run
could go on for hours, and stopping it meant interrupting whichever
pass it had reached. A run that answers one message and exits does
one thing that can be checked from outside, and leaves the decision
of when to run again to whatever runs it, whether that is an operator,
cron(8), or daemon(8).

Running lab-process-mail by hand now answers the oldest message and
nothing more.
